<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Happy Birthday to You</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">melody published <a href="/years/1893">1893</a> as &quot;Good Morning to All&quot;; birthday words in print by <a href="/years/1911">1911</a>-<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Happy Birthday to You&quot; is an American song sung to celebrate a person's birthday; the 1998 Guinness World Records called it the most recognized song in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-language">English language</a>, and its words have been translated into at least 18 languages.</p></div>
